Description: COSMIC desktop epoch-1.11.0, built for Debian 13 "trixie"
 The full COSMIC desktop stack from pop-os/cosmic-epoch tag epoch-1.11.0
 (compositor, panel, launcher, settings, files, terminal, editor, store and
 the rest) compiled on Debian 13 with the Rust toolchain from
 trixie-backports. Not an official Debian or System76 package.
 .
 Library dependencies are generated by dpkg-shlibdeps. The other
 dependencies follow the per-component Debian packaging of the same epoch,
 minus Pop!_OS-only packages that trixie does not have (pop-fonts,
 pop-icon-theme, pop-sound-theme, appstream-data-pop, adw-gtk3, casper).
 .
 The login screen (cosmic-greeter) is included but not enabled; choose
 "COSMIC" as the session in the existing display manager. To use it instead,
 install greetd and make cosmic-greeter.service the display manager:
   ln -sf /usr/lib/systemd/system/cosmic-greeter.service \
          /etc/systemd/system/display-manager.service
 The setup wizard runs once at each user's first COSMIC login. Its installer
 (OEM) mode, which creates the first user account, is not set up.
 .
 cosmic-osd is the polkit authentication agent, hence the Provides.
